1
00:00:00,020 --> 00:00:01,680
Tesla just made a car fly.

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:02,900
And hang upside down.

3
00:00:02,900 --> 00:00:04,100
How does it stick?

4
00:00:04,100 --> 00:00:05,540
Tesla says fans pull air

5
00:00:05,540 --> 00:00:06,740
from the gap underneath.

6
00:00:06,740 --> 00:00:07,600
Lower pressure there

7
00:00:07,600 --> 00:00:08,720
lets the surrounding air

8
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:10,380
press the car against the ramp.

9
00:00:10,380 --> 00:00:11,320
Once it's airborne,

10
00:00:11,320 --> 00:00:13,460
compressed-gas jets help rotate it upright

11
00:00:13,460 --> 00:00:14,680
and hold it steady.

12
00:00:14,680 --> 00:00:16,760
It even cleared a whole row of Teslas,

13
00:00:16,760 --> 00:00:17,960
Semi included.

14
00:00:17,960 --> 00:00:19,230
Zero to 60?

15
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:22,200
0.81 seconds, by Tesla's own test.

16
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:23,080
And flight?

17
00:00:23,080 --> 00:00:25,720
Tesla lists it only on the invite-only Rocket,

18
00:00:25,720 --> 00:00:28,160
which it says isn't approved for public roads.

19
00:00:28,160 --> 00:00:29,140
It flew.

20
00:00:29,140 --> 00:00:30,110
Road-ready?

21
00:00:30,140 --> 00:00:31,133
Not yet.
